<title>BELGIUM: EU clears 23.76 bln francs in aid to GAN.</title>
<headline>EU clears 23.76 bln francs in aid to GAN.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had cleared 20 billion francs of French state aid for GAN after Paris confirmed plans to privatise the loss-making insurer.</p>
<p>In taking its decision, the Commission also included in the total subsidies a state capital injection of 2.86 billion francs carried out in 1996.</p>
<p>It said the approval was made possible after the French government confirmed plans to privatise gan after it went through a drastic slimming course.</p>
<p>Under the strict restructuring plan approved by the EU, GAN must sell its banking unit CIC; divest its property units UIC and UIS; sell other holdings for a total value of 2.4 billion francs; and halve its foreign commercial interests.</p>
<p>The new French government of Socialist leader Lionel Jospin recently endorsed the planned privatisation of GAN which has lost 35 billion francs since 1992.</p>
</text>
